# Line endings.
#
# `npm run bootstrap` runs `bash scripts/bootstrap.sh`, and on Windows `bash` resolves to
# C:\WINDOWS\system32\bash.exe (WSL). A checked-out CRLF makes bash read the last token as
# `pipefail\r`, which fails with:
#
#     : invalid option name
#     line 2: set: pipefail
#
# Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` in its system config, so without this file every
# clone on Windows writes CRLF into the scripts and every bash entry point breaks. Pin the
# shell scripts to LF whatever the local setting is.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf

# Windows launchers, invoked as `powershell -File` / cmd; CRLF is native there.
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
